-- title:
--   Residue field of the supersingular prolongation from the affine chart
-- statement:
--   Let $q\ge 5$ be a prime and $M'$ a nonzero natural number not divisible by $q$, and let $A$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ lying over $q$ in the sense that $q$ is a nonunit of $A$. Let $W$ be a finite set of places of $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldC}(\mathrm{ResidueField}\,A, M')$ over the residue field of $A$ whose members are exactly the supersingular places $\mathrm{ssPlaces}\ q\ M'$, let $s\in W$, and assume $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}\ M'\le \mathrm{fieldBar}\ q\ M'$. Let $k_0\subseteq\overline{\mathbb Q}$ be an intermediate field over $\mathbb Q$ and $\pi_0\in k_0$ an element lying in $A$, such that the contraction $A\cap k_0$ is a henselian discrete valuation ring with maximal ideal generated by $\pi_0$ and algebraically closed residue field, and such that every $a\in A$ is congruent modulo the maximal ideal of $A$ to an element of $k_0\cap A$. Let $K_b$ be the trivial intermediate field $\bot$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ over $k_0$, and $A_b$ a valuation subring of $K_b$ whose elements are exactly those lying in $A$, assumed a henselian discrete valuation ring with maximal ideal generated by some $\varpi_b\ne 0$. Give $\mathrm{fieldBar}\ q\ M'$ the $k_0$-algebra structure coming from $\overline{\mathbb Q}$. The assertion is then: for every intermediate field $F_0$ of $\mathrm{fieldBar}\ q\ M'$ over $k_0$ and every valuation subring $W_0$ of $F_0$ such that the $k_0$-field generated by the image of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ together with $F_0$ is all of $\mathrm{fieldBar}\ q\ M'$, such that for $x\in k_0$ one has $x\in A$ iff the image of $x$ lies in $W_0$, such that $W_0$ is a discrete valuation ring, and such that the image of $\pi_0$ lies in $W_0$ and generates its maximal ideal; for every subring $B$ of $\mathrm{fieldBar}\ q\ M'$ carrying an $A_b$-algebra structure whose structure map is the inclusion $A_b\subseteq\overline{\mathbb Q}\to \mathrm{fieldBar}\ q\ M'$, with $B$ contained in $W_0$ (every element of $B$ lies in $F_0$ and there in $W_0$) and with $W_0$ the localisation of $B$ away from $\varpi_b$, i.e. $f\in W_0$ iff $fh=g$ for some $g,h\in B$ with the image of $\varpi_b$ not dividing $h$; and for every field $F_{ss}$ over the residue field of $A$ and every regular prolongation $R$ of $A$ to $\mathrm{fieldBar}\ q\ M'$ with residue field $F_{ss}$ — that is, a valuation subring $R.\mathrm{integers}$ contracting to $A$ on $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, together with a surjective ring homomorphism $R.\mathrm{residue}$ onto $F_{ss}$ whose kernel is the maximal ideal, compatible with reduction on $A$, and such that every nonzero $f$ has a scalar multiple with nonzero residue — satisfying $R.\mathrm{integers}\cap F_0=W_0$ and $B\subseteq R.\mathrm{integers}$: (a) every $x\in F_{ss}$ is of the form $x\cdot\overline h=\overline g$ with $g,h\in B$ and $\overline h\ne0$, where $\overline{\ \cdot\ }$ denotes $R.\mathrm{residue}$; and (b) for $b\in B$, $\overline b=0$ if and only if the image of $\varpi_b$ in $B$ divides $b$.
--
--   This identifies the reduced field $F_{ss}$ of the regular prolongation of $A$ through $W_0$ with the field of fractions of the special fibre $B/\varpi_b B$ of the affine chart $B$: the residue map is surjective up to denominators from $B$ and its kernel on $B$ is exactly $\varpi_b B$. It is used in the analysis of the supersingular reduction of the full-level modular curve, by the statements on supersingular discrete valuation rings, base-smooth point stalks and their localisations, and on Drinfeld inertia at the affine chart.
